<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Hostile medusa and lamia casting, 2026-09-23.

		An ability is invisible to the AI unless two things are true: the AbilityDef carries
		<aiCanUse>true</aiCanUse> (read by Ability.AICanTargetNow), and some think-tree node
		actually asks for it. `hostile` only marks the act as hostile. Vanilla has no generic
		"cast any hostile ability" node, so each hostile ability gets its own.

		Core's Abilities_Aggressive is the right tree: the raider DutyDefs reference it, and its
		only node is the AnimalWarcall one. These nodes are that shape. The leaf is our own
		PMM_Reptiles.JobGiver_AICastHostileAbility, because vanilla's JobGiver_AICastAbility is
		abstract - XML cannot build it, which is why no ability in the game uses the generic one.
		Ours picks the caster's best visible enemy and gives Ability.AICanTargetNow the last word,
		so aiCanUse, range, cooldown and the target rules still decide whether she casts.

		Inserted inside the tree's non-colonist conditional, so the player's own mamonos still cast
		only when told to. A non-colonist gets this tree through the duty she is on, which for our
		factions means raiders - a wild mamono casts nothing.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/ThinkTreeDef[defName="Abilities_Aggressive"]/thinkRoot/subNodes/li/subNodes</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="ThinkNode_ConditionalHasAbility">
				<ability>PMM_Ability_Petrify</ability>
				<subNodes>
					<li Class="ThinkNode_ConditionalHashIntervalTick">
						<interval>65</interval>
						<subNodes>
							<li Class="PMM_Reptiles.JobGiver_AICastHostileAbility">
								<abilityDef>PMM_Ability_Petrify</abilityDef>
							</li>
						</subNodes>
					</li>
				</subNodes>
			</li>
			<li Class="ThinkNode_ConditionalHasAbility">
				<ability>PMM_Ability_TailGrapple</ability>
				<subNodes>
					<li Class="ThinkNode_ConditionalHashIntervalTick">
						<interval>65</interval>
						<subNodes>
							<li Class="PMM_Reptiles.JobGiver_AICastHostileAbility">
								<abilityDef>PMM_Ability_TailGrapple</abilityDef>
							</li>
						</subNodes>
					</li>
				</subNodes>
			</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
